  "caption": "H-soft is nondominated within the registered regression menu, while its screening advantage over R-log remains uncertain. Its pooled RMSE is 4.6011 and its metal/nonmetal contributions to total MSE are 18.2920 and 2.8781. Each contribution is class-specific SSE divided by the total sample count; stacked sums equal pooled RMSE squared. Six numeric routes are shown for error decomposition, while the Pareto comparison uses only the four registered regressors. H-soft minus R-log has an EF difference of +1.6160 with the existing 95% paired AB percentile interval [-5.9951, 11.2022], conditional on frozen OOF predictions and prior selection without multiplicity correction. Pure screening routes have no assigned RMSE.",
